[size=6][b]R46 — The Homecoming Update[/b][/size]
[center][i]"It's good to be back."[/i][/center]

Celebrating coming back to Nexus, with a new home for your cooldowns and more ways to make your ASS your own.

[b]"Know what you need to know, and when you need to know it."[/b]
[img]https://i.imgur.com/j2QMCFL.gif[/img]

Cooldown dock or compact overview, game-font timers, separate inbound/impact countdowns, Eagle charge counts, and options for what stays visible. DBF overlays now follow native HUD visibility.

[b]"Fast - but still fair."[/b]
[img]https://i.imgur.com/0kZXJqm.gif[/img]

Wedge Wheel is the new-user default, with 50% default wedge opacity. Four optional equipped-stratagem hotkeys are unbound by default. Randomized input delay chooses 70–240 ms once per use.

Appearance and Blacklist are grouped in two columns. Hide blacklisted/cooldown list entries, configure timer positions, or reset a page to defaults. Use MCM 0.1.72 or newer for draft-aware conditional controls; DBF owns the rules.

[b]R46 notes:[/b] Keybindings list is now [b]List Select[/b]; Experimental layouts are under [b]Wedge Wheel[/b]. Select on Release defaults to Automatic for controller input. Native MBM does not currently apply author-defined mouse defaults—set Wheel Down, Wheel Up and Mouse 1 in its MODS tab. LLL supports guarded live reload; BSL and MDL remain restart-only. Existing saved preferences and binding IDs are retained.

[url=https://github.com/HWG90/DiversBestFriend/releases/tag/r46]R46 downloads and full release notes[/url]

[size=5][b]What it does[/b][/size]
Diver's Best Friend puts stratagem selection inside HELLDIVERS 2. Open the normal stratagem menu, choose an entry through a wheel or list, and ASS enters the code through the game's normal input path. You still equip and throw the beacon normally.

It reads live game data rather than trying to read the screen. There is no separate OCR program or external input helper to keep running while you play.

[url=https://github.com/HWG90/DiversBestFriend/releases/tag/r45]R45 downloads and full release notes[/url] | [url=https://github.com/HWG90/DiversBestFriend/blob/r45/docs/INSTALLATION.md]Installation and controls[/url] | [url=https://github.com/HWG90/DiversBestFriend/issues]Report an issue[/url]

[size=5][b]Pick your layout[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Native wheel:[/b] eight slots, mouse or stick pointing, and Next/Previous paging.
[*][b]Keybindings list:[/b] Next/Previous and Confirm, following list order and wrapping at either end. Camera control remains available.
[*][b]Experimental Cards:[/b] up to sixteen native stratagem cards arranged in a circle.
[*][b]Experimental Expanded wedges:[/b] up to sixteen entries on a single wheel.
[/list]
Radial layouts retain the original top-left stratagem list. Camera control returns when the menu closes.

[b]Select on Release[/b] is optional and off by default. With a Hold menu binding, point at an entry and release to select. Return the pointer to the center before releasing to cancel. List mode uses Confirm.

[b]Input interval[/b] controls the delay between code directions: 0-250 ms, default 70 ms. It applies to both Confirm and Select on Release.

Native and expanded wheels dim entries during delivery or cooldown and show the selected entry's remaining time. Exhausted single-use entries stay dim and cannot be selected again. Scrambled-code handling follows the currently required sequence; normal game availability still applies.

[size=5][b]R45 - Plays Nicely With Others[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]HUD Plus 0.2.8:[/b] its competing stratagem list and picker yield while ASS controls selection. Other HUD Plus features remain active. HUD Plus resumes its list behavior when ASS is disabled or recovering.
[*][b]Custom Stratagem Compendium 0.4.1 / HD2Runtime 0.40.0:[/b] custom call-in codes work with Confirm and Select on Release, with ownership and code-content checks retained.
[*][b]Single-use availability:[/b] fixes entries such as Shredder continuing to look available after use. Becoming unavailable after arming also cancels release selection.
[*][b]Foliage Pass-Through 1.0:[/b] recognizes its exact projectile collision-template change so Runtime can validate custom gas-barrage and cluster-launcher donors. Other changes remain checked.
[*]Includes R42 recovery for recognized temporary HUD failures: cancel pending input, restore UI/camera control, then close and reopen the stratagem menu to resume. Held inputs are not replayed.
[/list]
[b]HUD Plus, Custom Stratagem Compendium, HD2Runtime and Foliage Pass-Through are optional compatibility targets.[/b] You do not need them to use ASS. Foliage can be on or off; restart after changing it.

[size=5][b]Requirements[/b][/size]
Install these separately. They are not bundled.
[list]
[*][b]One compatible loader:[/b] [url=https://github.com/CowboyBingus/BingusSharedLoader/releases/latest]Bingus Shared Loader[/url] / API 1 for the BSL package; MDL API 2 for the MDL package; or [url=https://github.com/HWG90/LLL/releases]LLL R30+[/url] for the LLL package.
[*][url=https://github.com/CowboyBingus/ModBindingsMenu/releases/latest]Mod Bindings Menu[/url] v2 or newer / API 1.
[*][url=https://github.com/CowboyBingus/ModOptionsMenu]Mod Options Menu[/url], available through your chosen loader's shared-addon compatibility route.
[*]HELLDIVERS 2 on Windows/Steam, supported build 25480438.
[/list]
[url=https://www.nexusmods.com/helldivers2/mods/17157]Mod Configuration Menu[/url] is optional. It provides additional blacklist entries; you can use the core selection features without it. Neither the old external Stratagem Wheel app nor the Equipped Stratagems exporter is required.

[size=5][b]Installation - choose ONE file[/b][/size]
[b]BSL edition - DiversBestFriend-R45-BSL.zip[/b]
With the game closed, import the ZIP into Arsenal, enable it and deploy. Follow your loader's startup-priority instructions.

[b]LLL edition - DiversBestFriend-R45-LLL.zip[/b]
With the game closed, extract the complete [b]divers_best_friend[/b] folder into:
[code]%LOCALAPPDATA%/LLL/Helldivers2/Mods[/code]
Enable it in LLL. Keep the required binding/options dependencies available.

[b]MDL edition - DiversBestFriend-R45-MDL.zip[/b]
With the game closed, extract the complete [b]divers_best_friend[/b] folder into:
[code]%LOCALAPPDATA%/MDL/Helldivers2/Mods[/code]
Enable it in MDL API 2. This adapter has passed isolated startup/lifecycle tests; MDL gameplay has not been verified.

[b]Install one ASS revision and one loader variant.[/b] Remove or disable the old ASS archive provider before switching to loose LLL/MDL files. Keep the full packaged folder together. Existing binding IDs and saved options are retained. Restart after updates; ASS is restart-only and does not support hot-reload or live provider switching.

[size=5][b]First launch[/b][/size]
[list=1]
[*]Open [b]MODS > Diver's Best Friend[/b], choose your selection mode and Apply.
[*]Configure [b]Next stratagem[/b], [b]Previous stratagem[/b] and [b]Confirm stratagem[/b] in the native bindings menu's MODS tab. Mouse defaults are Wheel Down, Wheel Up and Mouse 1.
[*]In a mission, open the normal stratagem menu and select an available entry. Keep the menu open until code entry finishes, then throw the beacon normally.
[*]For release selection, enable [b]Select on Release[/b] and use a Hold stratagem-menu binding. Return to center before releasing to cancel.
[/list]

